## Object-Oriented Design Principles

| Principle       | Description                                                                 |
|----------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| **Abstraction**    | Shows only essential features of an object while hiding internal complexities.  |
| **Encapsulation**  | Restricts direct access to an object’s data and allows controlled interaction through methods. |
| **Modularity**     | Breaks down a program into smaller, self-contained units that can be developed and maintained independently. |
